A||||3||WKDFIRO||Cadillac Catalytic Convertors||||6||
Z||000000||WKDFIRO||02-05-2001||07:28 AM||||Since most of my friends have Flowmasters with 2.5 inch exhaust, I decided to try something a little different hopeing for a slightly different sound but still having the same snarl and cam burble.<P>I had never heard of anyone else doing it so I figured I would do it and find out. I had a 2.5 inch mandrel bent exhaust put in from the cat back with no muffler. I was betting on the cat taking up most of the loudness and the 4.5 inch glasspack exhaust tips would be my Plan B if it got too loud.<P>What I hadn't anticipated was that the Cat was old and totally blown out hollow. Great sound at idle, but howling resonance inside on the freeway! Without the glasspack tips I wouldn't dare go out on to the streets! Even got pulled over!<P>So I went back to my exhaust guy (he did the exhaust work for Fiero Motorsports) who chuckled when he saw me come back and I asked what options I had. He said that Cadillacs have a 2.5 inch cat/muffler combo to quiet them down before it goes to the muffler. So tomorrow the Cadillac Catalytic Convertor (try saying that 3 times fast!)goes on. <P>Right now the exhaust at idle sounds like a cammy boat motor with the exhaust tip resonators. So I thought I would share this information. I love the 2.5 inch exhaust even with ported manifolds. Perhaps the cat will give me just a little bit of backpreasure to help out the scavenge effect. That was my greatest concern was to lose too much on the bottom end from not enough back preasure.<P>Hopefully good news tomorrow! ||||reg||6
Z||000001||86se/lambo||02-06-2001||01:31 AM||||how about a cat from chris west..$78..your system sounds alot like mine. have you ever seen the one forom borla that is designed for the camaro..it has multiple plates of different diameters to adjust the sound quality...ask the muffler guy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||02-06-2001||10:55 PM||||Well unfortunately, the catalytic convertor did tone down the noise at idle but did little for the resonance in the cabin. Proof positive that Cats make lousy mufflers. Even the quietest catalytic converter (with a built-in muffler) cannot quiet down a 2.5 inch exhaust. <P>My experiment is over and its time for muffler. At least if anyone wonders if this exhaust is the way to go there is now someone who has been there and done that. <P>The exhaust shop that helped me with my experiment was the Weld Shop in Orange County, CA (714-744-5854). They have done many Fieros with Flowmasters and Steve is a good sport for going along with my half cracked idea. The least I can do is give him a plug. <P>If you do give him a call tell him that Anthony sent ya!<P> <p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||02-07-2001||04:53 PM||||I just got a Spintech 331SC with 2.5" in and dual 2" out. 13.25" in length or about 1.25" wider than the stock Fiero. Should fit in the same space. I opt'd for the 2" outlets rather than 2.5" outlets to keep the volume down (Spintech's recommendation). About $140 out the door in California. I hope to get it in this weekend. The are willing to crank them out for Fiero's replacements.  <P>I asked for a quiet/flowing muffler (mutually exclusive). I'll see how it does on both. If I can keep it below 2PSI and still hear myself think, I'll be happy. It's one heavy muffler.||||reg||1
